course: dictionary
lesson: 11253
title: Worst and its phrases
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Worst means the most bad of all. It sits at the top of a scale: bad, worse, worst. A bad day is not nice, a worse day is nicer, and the worst day is the one that is more bad than all the others.
explain: Context shows you how worst is used. «After your first netball training or a long cross-country, your legs may ache so much the stairs feel like a mountain, usually worst one or two days later.» The ache is at its most painful one or two days later, so worst means most painful of all.
explain: Worst often appears in phrases, and each phrase has its own meaning. «At worst» means if things go as badly as they can. «If the worst comes to the worst» means if the very worst happens. Learn the whole phrase together, not just the single word.
fact: Worst is the top form of bad: bad, worse, worst.
fact: «The worst» means the most bad thing that can happen.
fact: «At worst» means if things go as badly as they can.
fact: Worst can also be an adverb, meaning most badly, as in «usually worst one or two days later».
fact: In maths, a worst case problem asks you to count the unluckiest picks first, then add one to be sure.
exercise: «...your legs may ache so much the stairs feel like a mountain, usually worst one or two days later.» When does the ache usually feel worst? | Before you have ever played netball | During the very first minute of training | *One or two days later | The ache always stops at once
exercise: Which phrase means if things go as badly as they can? | Worse and worse | Worst case | *At worst | The worst part
exercise: In a worst case maths problem, what do you count first? | *The unluckiest picks | The picks you like best | The luckiest picks | The total number of picks in the bag
test: Which word completes the scale: bad, worse, ___? | *worst | quietest | brightest | nicest
test: «If the worst comes to the worst», what does the phrase mean? | If the weather is bad for a day | If the worst is already over | *If the very worst happens | If everything goes perfectly
exam: «The worst of the cold is over.» What does this tell you? | Winter is only just beginning | The worst storm is coming next | *The most bad part of the cold has passed | The cold is at its strongest right now
